# Line endings are part of the build output here, not a cosmetic preference.
#
# sbom.cdx.json records a SHA-256 for every shipped file, and the release
# packages are meant to rebuild byte-identically from a tag. With core.autocrlf
# on Windows the working tree had CRLF while Linux checked out LF, so the same
# commit produced different hashes on different machines - which CI caught by
# failing the SBOM check. An integrity manifest that depends on who built it is
# not an integrity manifest.
#
# Forcing LF in the working tree on every platform makes the hashes, the zips
# and the checksums properties of the commit instead of the operating system.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
